    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="0917" n="907" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg907"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">195.91/2–1049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-10T10:00:00+08:00">February 10,
                            1949—10 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 9—11:53 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>458. APL<anchor n="83" xml:id="d845-f1"/> ship <hi rendition="#italic">President
                        Fillmore</hi> due Tangku about February 18. ConGen Peiping<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d845-f2"/> has inquired as to identity consignees and description
                    cargo. APL Shanghai requests assistance ConGen Peiping ascertaining from
                    Communist authorities possibility entrance Tangku and any unusual entry
                    requirements. This may be good opportunity maneuver Communist authorities into
                    permitting Shanghai communicate ConGen Tientsin,<anchor n="85" xml:id="d845-f3"
                    /> assuming Communists are anxious for cargo to be delivered. Department may
                    wish consider advisability requesting APL not to send ship Tangku unless master
                    receives advance permission communicate with ConGen Tientsin and obtain shipping
                    services normally accorded by consular officers to ships of American
                    registry.</p>
                <pb facs="0918" n="908" xml:id="pg908"/>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated office [of] Embassy [at] Canton 35. Department please
                    pass Peiping as 33, Tientsin as 22.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
